==Dutch==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|nl|dum|hebben}}, from {{inh|nl|odt|hebben}}, from {{inh|nl|gmw-pro|*habbjan}}, from {{inh|nl|gem-pro|*habjaną}}, from {{der|nl|ine-pro|*keh₂p-||to grasp}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|nl|/ˈɦɛbə(n)/}}
* {{audio|nl|Nl-hebben.ogg}}
* {{hyphenation|nl|heb|ben}}
* {{rhymes|nl|ɛbən|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{nl-verb}}

# {{lb|nl|transitive}} to [[have]], to [[possess]], [[own]], [[hold]]
#: {{syn|nl|bezitten}}
#: {{uxi|nl|'''Hebt''' u een minuut?|Do you '''have''' a minute?}}
# {{lb|nl|transitive|medicine}} to be [[afflict]]ed with a [[disease]]
#: {{uxi|nl|Ik '''heb''' griep.|I '''have''' the flu.}}
# {{lb|nl|auxiliary}} {{non-gloss definition|Used to form the [[perfect tense]] of the [[active voice]] of most verbs, together with a [[past participle]].}}
#: {{uxi|nl|Ik '''heb''' het koekje opgegeten.|I '''have''' eaten the biscuit.}}
#: {{uxi|nl|Ze '''hadden''' hun auto net gewassen.|They '''had''' only just washed their car.}}
#: {{uxi|nl|Hij '''heeft''' naar huis moeten lopen.|He '''has''' had to walk home.}}
#: {{uxi|nl|Ik '''heb''' hem horen praten.|I '''have''' heard him speak.}}
#: {{uxi|nl|Dat '''had''' je moeten doen.|You should '''have''' done that.}}
# {{lb|nl|auxiliary|with {{m|nl|te}}}} [[must]], to be [[obliged]] to, to [[be]] to
#: {{syn|nl|moeten}}
#: {{uxi|nl|Daar '''hebben''' we ons bij neer te leggen.|We '''must''' accept that.}}

